exercises.task:
Implement `solve(a, b)` (both 2-D tensors):
(1) if `b`'s rows equal `a`'s columns → return `tf.matMul(a, b)`;
(2) else if `b`'s COLUMNS equal `a`'s columns → return `tf.matMul(a, tf.transpose(b))`;
(3) otherwise call `tf.matMul(a, b)` anyway WITHOUT try/catch, so the real error propagates.

