exercises.task:
Implement `solve(q, k)` → `{ unscaledMax, unscaledMin, scaledMax, scaledMin }`, plain numbers:
- compute raw scores `Q·Kᵀ`;
- `unscaled*` = max/min entry of `softmax(scores)`;
- `scaled*` = max/min entry of `softmax(scores / √d)` with `d = k.shape[1]`.
With the test inputs (d = 16, √d = 4): unscaled softmax collapses to a near one-hot, scaled stays soft — the numbers must show it.

